$.#587
|  To draw once again from coding analogies,
|  programming language semantics is concerned with the binding
|  of values to symbols --- when those "markings" start and
|  cease to be appropriate --- as well as polymorphic
|  definition of multiple procedures with thesymbol
|  but different parameter types, and other type-related
.  concerns
asl-sentence-text $# 587 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 583 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 583 104952 1982 10 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 583 105279 1987 21 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#588
|  Code syntax addresses such issues as
|  expression boundaries, storage-duration scope, and "sequence points", indicating
|  which values are parameters for which function-calls as
|  well as, potentially, the order of procedures' side-effects
|  (particularly when a prior effect could be "visible" to
.  a future subroutine)
asl-sentence-text $# 588 ;.

asl-new-sentence 4# 584 ;.
asl-sentence-switch-pos 4#/4 584 105280 1987 22 ;.
asl-sentence--end-pos 4#/4 584 105503 1990 63 ;.
asl-sentence-end-punctuation $ . ;.
$.#589
|  Syntactic and
|  semantic systems are necessary to ensure that high-level code
|  maps (properly) to a "push/transfer"-like stack representation, ensuring that
.  all procedures' type and precondition contracts are guaranteed
asl-sentence-text $# 589 ;.

